      "role": "user",
      "content": "the utilitarian thing makes sense but it feels a bit like a loophole to just say \"it depends on the math.\" if you're looking at it from a purely ethical standpoint, wouldn't the most logical framework be to prioritize the spread of democratic values and human rights over old school ideas like sovereignty? like, shouldn't protecting people from tyranny be considered a universal moral truth that outweighs a country's right to be left alone?",
